Which might be a bit tricky if you don't know much about that...

I've put the syntax file using the name des.vim into vim's installation
directory (in my case /usr/share/vim/vim##/syntax/, '##' is version no),
and added into my vim profile ~/.vimrc the lines (in given order)

   au BufNewFile,BufRead *.des   setf des
   syntax on

(The reason is that changing the global vim filetype file is deprecated.)

